# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
target/
out/
build/
*.class
*.war

# Safe as a blanket rule: nothing in this repo is a committed jar. The Maven wrapper is
# `distributionType=only-script` (see .mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.properties), so it downloads Maven
# itself and needs no maven-wrapper.jar — a fresh clone still runs ./mvnw.
*.jar
.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar

# Maven plugin leftovers that land next to the POM rather than in target/.
dependency-reduced-pom.xml
.flattened-pom.xml
pom.xml.versionsBackup
release.properties
buildNumber.properties

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# JVM crash and profiling dumps
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A heap dump from an OOM during a load test is ~1GB of binary. It has happened to people.
*.hprof
hs_err_pid*
replay_pid*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IDE and editor
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.vscode/
.vs/
*.suo
.settings/
.classpath
.project
*.swp
*~

# Merge and patch debris. `git add -A` after a conflict is how these reach a public repo.
*.orig
*.rej
*.bak

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs and scratch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/
tmp/
.tmp/
scratch/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and local overrides
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The committed defaults are deliberately fake — `local-dev-key`, `sentinel`/`sentinel` — and the
# LLM key defaults to the `not-configured` placeholder that RcaConfig recognises. Anything real
# arrives through one of these, and none of them belong in a public repo.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
application-local.yml
application-local.yaml

# Helm value overrides. `--set sentinel.llm.apiKey=...` on the command line leaves no file, but a
# values-local.yaml with a real Groq key is the obvious next step and would be committed by accident.
values-local.yaml
values.local.yaml
values-secret*.yaml

# Certificates and keystores.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks

# Cluster credentials. `kind get kubeconfig > kubeconfig` is a very easy habit.
kubeconfig
*.kubeconfig

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docker and Kubernetes local state
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
docker-compose.override.yml
docker-compose.override.yaml

# Rendered Helm output and packaged charts.
#
# k8s/helm/sentinel/files/ is deliberately NOT ignored. Those are committed copies of the recording
# rules, the dashboards and the baseline k6 script, because Helm cannot read above the chart root
# and `helm install ./k8s/helm/sentinel` has to work from a fresh clone with no sync step.
# `make k8s-check` is what keeps them from drifting.
rendered/
*.tgz
k8s/helm/*/charts/
k8s/helm/*/Chart.lock

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Load test scratch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# docs/LOAD_TEST_RESULTS.raw.md is intentionally NOT ignored — raw benchmark output is evidence, and
# a results table with no raw output behind it is just a claim. It is regenerated by every run of
# scripts/load-test.sh, so commit it when it corresponds to the numbers in LOAD_TEST_RESULTS.md and
# not before.
k6-summary.json
*.k6-summary.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent tooling
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local tool configuration, not part of the project. Nothing in the build, the demo or CI reads it.
.claude/

# The build spec Claude Code reads. Kept local rather than committed — it is scaffolding for how the
# project was built, not documentation of what it does; README.md and docs/ are that. Was listed
# under "Build output" but had been tracked since the initial commit, so the rule never applied
# until `git rm --cached` untracked it.
CLAUDE.md
